# The Test Cabinet — auth service environment file (`tcab-auth-service`).
#
# Copy this file to `.env.auth` and fill in real values:
#
#     cp .env.auth.example .env.auth
#
# The auth service loads `.env.auth` on startup (searching the working directory
# and its parents). Variables already exported in your shell take precedence
# over the file, so a systemd unit or container can export them directly.
#
# `.env.auth` is gitignored; this `.env.auth.example` is committed with
# placeholder values only. Never put a real secret in `.env.auth.example`.

# ── Core ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# Address the Axum server binds. Bind to a private-network IP (e.g. a Tailscale
# address) in production — the service is reached only over the private network.
# Default: 127.0.0.1:8789
#TCAB_AUTH_BIND=127.0.0.1:8789

# Database connection URL. The scheme selects the backend (via SeaORM):
#   - SQLite (local/dev): a file URL, created if missing with `?mode=rwc`. This
#     is the auth service's OWN database, separate from the backend's.
#   - PostgreSQL (deployment): a `postgres://` URL to a managed instance, which
#     also makes the auth service stateless (no local DB file or single-replica
#     caveat). The schema is migrated automatically on startup.
# Default: sqlite://./tcab-auth.sqlite?mode=rwc
#TCAB_AUTH_DATABASE_URL=sqlite://./tcab-auth.sqlite?mode=rwc
#TCAB_AUTH_DATABASE_URL=postgres://tcab:password@db.internal:5432/tcab-auth

# ── Telemetry (OpenTelemetry / OTLP) ─────────────────────────────────────────
#
# Telemetry is OPT-IN. With OTEL_EXPORTER_OTLP_ENDPOINT unset (the default), the
# auth service logs to stdout — no exporter, no collector needed. Set the
# endpoint to export traces, metrics, and logs over OTLP/HTTP.
#
# The auth service runs INSIDE the devcontainer, so it reaches the local Grafana
# LGTM stack by its compose service DNS name. (From the HOST you would use
# http://localhost:4318 instead — see .devcontainer/docker-compose.yml.)
#OTEL_EXPORTER_OTLP_ENDPOINT=http://lgtm:4318

# The binaries always export over HTTP/protobuf; this is the SDK default when
# the endpoint is the :4318 HTTP port, so it normally needs no override.
#OTEL_EXPORTER_OTLP_PROTOCOL=http/protobuf

# OTel service.name. Defaults to the value the binary seeds (`tcab-auth-service`);
# uncomment only to override.
#OTEL_SERVICE_NAME=tcab-auth-service

# Sets the `deployment.environment.name` resource attribute. Default: local
#TCAB_ENV=local
